Selected Idea
-------------

Decoding the Project Gutenberg license: what you can and must do with a public-domain eBook
Use the Gettysburg Address eBook as a concrete example to explain the Project Gutenberg License's core permissions and obligations: what distributors and users are allowed to do with public-domain texts (copy, modify, redistribute, create derivatives) and which mandatory conditions accompany that freedom (retain the full license, display a required notice, format and distribution rules, refund/replacement rights).

